name: Logistics cargo theft
tagline: "A seeded cargo-theft Link Analysis demo - an inside job, a stop hotspot and a fictitious carrier, planted among 12 900 trips, 900 drivers and 120 carriers with benign look-alikes"
description: "The logistics cargo-theft Link Analysis demo as a Space Template, Basic tier. Eight synthetic feeds (carrier, driver, place, shipment, trip, stop, warehouse_scan, loss_report; 12 months landed from 2025-10-01 in data/inbox, the next month in data/staged; 120 carriers, 900 drivers, 12 warehouses and 133 places on the road, about 12 900 trips with one shipment each, 13 000 GPS stops, 46 000 warehouse scans and 63 loss reports) are landed by eight Collectors and Pipelines. The logistics_links Job folds them into ONE link Dataset (src, dst, kind, ts, amount, event_date, via) of seven link kinds; the logistics_screen_links Job derives the three cargo-security screens the saved views read. Planted stories (ground truth: tools/gen-la-logistics-data.ground-truth.json; pinned by LogisticsLinksJobGoldenTest and tools/gen-la-logistics-data.test.mjs): 12 short-delivered loads that share one two-driver team, 10 of them scanned out by the same night-shift scanner; 9 high-value trucks robbed while standing at one unofficial lay-by; a carrier registered three weeks earlier, sharing a dismissed driver's phone, whose 5 high-value loads never arrive. Benign look-alikes that must not join a story: the busiest driver on the busiest route with 2 losses, the official services where about 240 trucks a year take a long break, and a new insured owner-operator that delivers. Three saved views. Basic tier: runs on every edition, Basic included. Advanced tier, in the same template and inert on Basic: Demo Users and roles (config/demo-users.toon, roles.toon: logistics.analyst lead, logistics.manager second approver, logistics.reviewer read-only, logistics.outsider not a member, admin), four-eyes above a fan-out of 2000 and Drafts (link-analysis.toon), the logistics_new_carrier_counts and logistics_new_carrier_alerts Jobs and the Alert Rule logistics_high_value_trip_new_carrier (a high-value trip assigned to a carrier under 60 days old that is not insured: on the shipped data it counts the fictitious carrier's 5 loads, out of 16 high-value trips given to carriers under 60 days old; the new insured owner-operator's 9 are not counted; unarmed on Basic). Investigations, members, an Entity List, a Case, a held four-eyes expand and a Draft are runtime state: run `node tools/seed-la-logistics.mjs --apply` on an Advanced or Preview build with Demo Auth. Synthetic data only."
minEdition: basic
icon: heroicons_outline:truck
contents[7]: "8 Collectors + Pipelines + Datasets (12 months landed, 1 month staged)", "logistics_links Job + Dataset (7 link kinds, via) and the logistics_screen_links Dataset of three cargo-security screens", "3 saved views (inside job, stop hotspots, new carriers)", "3 planted stories with benign look-alikes", "Ground truth and golden tests in the repository", "Advanced tier: 5 Demo Users + role table, four-eyes (inert on Basic)", "Advanced tier: Alert Rule on a high-value trip given to an uninsured carrier under 60 days old (counts Job + evaluate Job, unarmed on Basic)"
